        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Issue Handling & Rectification Strategy\n",
        "Based on our profiling results, we apply the following treatment and transformation strategies:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Issue Identified | Location / Severity | Action Taken | Justification |\n",
        "| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n",
        "| **Data Types** | `released_date`, `last_updated`, `shutdown` | Converted string objects to `datetime64[ns]` with `errors='coerce'`. | Enables arithmetic time-delta calculations for app operational lifespans. |\n",
        "| **Structural Missingness** | `shutdown` column (~62.8% null) | Created binary flag `is_active` (1 if null, 0 if present). Imputed fallback references for time computations. | Missing `shutdown` indicates the application is **active**. Dropping these rows would destroy active app data. |\n",
        "| **Missing Text Strings** | `purpose` & `agency` | Filled `purpose` nulls with `'Not Specified'`. | Preserves row records while avoiding null errors in text analysis. |\n",
        "| **Category Formatting** | `operating_system`, `agency` | Standardized case casing and trimmed trailing/leading whitespace. | Prevents splitting identical categories (e.g., `'Ios'` vs `'iOS'`) during grouping. |\n",
        "| **System Date Errors** | Calculated `lifespan_days` | Dropped records where `lifespan_days < 0`. | Negative lifespans indicate erroneous upstream release or update timestamps. |\n",
        "| **Outlier Handling** | `lifespan_days` | Detected via $1.5 \\times IQR$ upper bound ($4213.6\\text{ days}$) and **capped** upper values. | Long-standing public applications are legitimate historical records, not measurement noise. Capping prevents extreme skew without losing sample size. |"
      ]
